# MANDATORY: TRANSOVO Internationalization & Localization Standards (Guide #11)

**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-INTERNATIONALIZATION-LOCALIZATION-STANDARDS.md`

## Hard requirement

All user-facing strings and locale-sensitive formatting **MUST** follow this guide. Read before adding copy or format logic.

## Non-negotiables

- **No hardcoded user-facing strings** in components without i18n architecture path defined in guide.
- **Pluralization, gender, context** handled correctly — not string concatenation hacks.
- Numbers, currency, dates use **locale-aware formatting**.
- Layout must tolerate **text expansion** (German, etc.) — no fixed-width truncation of labels.
- RTL readiness per guide where applicable.
- Don't embed English-only error messages from APIs without translation layer plan.
- Locale/timezone preferences persist and affect display consistently.

## On conflict

Date/time guide (Guide #10) for temporal specifics; governance for product scope.
